{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790349524,"nonce":"nbPY0S5h4iuY6FesArrzgENhKvI=","title":"zynml run exits 0 without running anything when main fails analysis","message":"Lowering drops a function whose body fails analysis with a warning (crates/compiler/src/lowering.rs:2681), and ZynML::run_file (crates/zynml/src/lib.rs:521) calls main only when it is among the loaded functions, else returns Ok. So a program whose main does not type-check runs nothing and exits 0:\n\n    import prelude\n    struct V {\n        x: i64\n    }\n    impl Add\u003cV\u003e for V {\n        def add(self, other: V): V {\n            return V { x: self.x + other.x }\n        }\n    }\n    def main(): i64 {\n        let c = V { x: 1 } + V { x: 2 }\n        println(c.x)\n        return c.x\n    }\n\nstderr carries \"[LOWERING] skipping function 'main' due to analysis error: Cannot access fields on non-struct type: Unknown\" among the prelude's duplicate-declaration warnings; stdout is empty and the status is 0. An entry point that fails to build should be an error with the analysis message. NUC x86_64, main 19697230.","files":null}]}